  "query_preview": "..Ridging is building into the Southwest as a \nshortwave moves into west Texas. High pressure will stay in \nplace over the region into next week leading to a slow warmup \nand dry conditions. Highs from central Pima County westward will\nbe a few degrees above normal and from Tucson east highs will \nbe around normal to just below normal through Monday. The \ncoolest temps will be east of Tucson. By the middle of next week\ntemps will be above normal area wide. A backdoor cold front \nmoving into the region today will be the reason for the temp \ndisparity across the CWA. At the same time a strong easterly \nsurface pressure gradient sets up leading to breezy easterly \nwinds through Monday. Winds will increase starting early this \nmorning with some higher elevation obs already seeing gusty \neasterly winds. Expect speeds generally 15-25 mph with gusts \n30-40 mph. High elevation areas could see brief and localized \nhigher wind gusts. Winds today will peak late morning into the \nearly afternoon, taper some in the afternoon, then increase \nagain overnight. The strongest winds will be in southern Cochise\nCounty and the Gila River Valley. Winds look to be strongest \ntoday and Sunday with the gradient weakening by Monday. Models \nshow another easterly surface gradient setting up late next \nweek.",
